   "date": "2017-09-09T19:46:51Z",
   "subject": "Re: Shiny DT slice date/time values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">There are 2 minor issues with your formatDate params:<div><br></div><div>- options should be in an object/list by themselves (see <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/toLocaleTimeString\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/toLocaleTimeString&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388906741000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0wM2wcNx9wvWcIeEVS1Jnp\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/toLocaleTimeString</a>)</div><div>- the JSON serializer in DT uses R&#39;s built-in TRUE/FALSE logicals, not &#39;true&#39; / &#39;false&#39; strings</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">formatDate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;toLocaleTimeString&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>           </span><span style=\"color:#008\">params</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;en-US&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hour </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;numeric&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> minute </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;numeric&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> hour12 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>Btw, that DataTable slice looks like it clones the DataTable, probably not what you were thinking</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "8qtcAy4WAQAJ",
   "from": "Scott Goley",
   "author": "e5563c64d65403a1",
   "date": "2017-09-13T14:05:25Z",
   "subject": "Re: Shiny DT slice date/time values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, sorry - that must have been from a copy / paste from one of my older versions but I am using R logicals and I do have the param options in a sub list. <div><br></div><div>Can you confirm that even with those options specified, it still populates seconds, AM/PM, and Time Zone?</div><div><br></div><div>And yes, slice from DataTables isn&#39;t what I meant exactly. Something more like <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String/slice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String/slice&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388906742000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2xXq39R8KoQDvbA08hpmTy\">String.prototype.slice()</a>. </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks Greg. </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Saturday, September 9, 2017 at 3:46:51 PM UTC-4, Greg L wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">There are 2 minor issues with your formatDate params:<div><br></div><div>- options should be in an object/list by themselves (see <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/toLocaleTimeString\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/toLocaleTimeString&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388906742000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-5FrY7sshOpQ1v0_o9ppr\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/toLocaleTimeString</a>)</div><div>- the JSON serializer in DT uses R&#39;s built-in TRUE/FALSE logicals, not &#39;true&#39; / &#39;false&#39; strings</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">formatDate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;toLocaleTimeString&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>           </span><span style=\"color:#008\">params</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;en-US&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hour </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;numeric&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> minute </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;numeric&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> hour12 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>Btw, that DataTable slice looks like it clones the DataTable, probably not what you were thinking</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
